WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.360
To help explain why this is all such a

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.080
big deal in the UK, and why so many

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.159
people are angry, let's dial it back to

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.880
May 2020.

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:29.680
More than 36,000 people had already died

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.759
of COVID. Intensive care units were full

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.600
and lockdown rules were strict.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:35.759
Socialising indoors with anyone from

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.320
outside your household was banned, so

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:41.040
families and friends were kept apart.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.600
In mid-May, the government

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.240
announced a slight relaxation in the

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.640
rules, and ministers went on TV to push

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.719
the message. 

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.520
But it turns out that on the same day as

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.599
that TV appearance, a senior official in

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.760
Downing Street invited more than 100

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:13.599
staff to socially distanced drinks in

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.640
the garden and told them to "bring your

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.480
own booze".

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.480
And Boris Johnson has acknowledged that

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.200
he was there, but that he thought it was

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.280
for work. 

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.440
But that's just one example.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.560
The report that's just come out lists 16

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.519
gatherings.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:49.120
There were goodbye drinks for staff, a

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.120
birthday party for the prime minister

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.800
and two gatherings in Downing Street the

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.599
night before the funeral for Prince

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:59.599
Philip—where the Queen sat alone as she

00:02:55.599 --> 00:03:01.519
buried her husband of 73 years.

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:04.239
Now this report was done by a Downing

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:06.239
Street bureaucrat—Sue Gray. 

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:12.480
And her investigation became a big part of the

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:14.400
story because once Boris Johnson stopped

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.360
denying outright that any rules had been

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.280
broken,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.480
waiting for Sue Gray's report kind of

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.120
became his main defence. 

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.760
The thing is, we still don't actually have

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.920
Sue Gray's full report. So far it's just

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.360
an "update", and that's because the police

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.480
decided to launch their own

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.560
investigation,

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.319
and they asked Sue Gray to hold back on

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.159
any juicy details so it wouldn't

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:54.080
compromise their work. 

00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:56.000
We know now that police are looking into

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.480
12 of the gatherings, and the prime

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.640
minister attended at least two of those.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:03.519
According to media reports, he was at

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.680
others, too. And another thing Sue Gray

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:08.239
gave the police: a pile of evidence,

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.920
including 300 photographs. 

00:04:22.479 --> 00:04:27.040
It's a lifeline the

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:29.199
prime minister appears to be hanging

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.759
onto, and that his opponents are

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:34.800
criticising. 

00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:02.880
So, what now? Well, the police

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:05.199
investigation could drag on for months.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.600
But in the end the worst anyone will get

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:09.840
for breaking COVID rules is a fine, so no

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.240
one's facing jail time. But Boris

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.560
Johnson's job is on the line because his

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.560
own Conservative MPs could decide to

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.880
kick him out. That would involve what's

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:22.240
called a vote of no confidence. To hold

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.960
one, 15% of Conservative MPs—so 54

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.360
out of 359—have to write a letter to the

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.880
head of a special committee. So far only

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.800
a few have said publicly that they've

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.880
done that. But the process happens in

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:35.440
secret, so we're never quite sure of the

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.600
numbers. If a vote does happen, Johnson

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:41.199
would need a simple majority to keep his

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.560
job. But again, that's if it even happens.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.919
So, he's promised to make some changes and follow

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.600
Sue Gray's recommendations, including

00:05:55.919 --> 00:06:01.759
changing the management structure in

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:03.600
No.10. 

00:06:14.319 --> 00:06:19.280
And that's really a big part of what this comes down to for

00:06:16.319 --> 00:06:21.759
Boris Johnson—his style of leadership.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.960
But Conservative MPs are now weighing up

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:57.759
whether "Partygate" and all the public

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.400
outrage has damaged the Boris brand so

00:06:57.759 --> 00:07:02.400
much that he's now become a liability. 

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:50.319
And that's something that Boris Johnson and his allies are

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:52.240
really trying to push, basically saying

00:07:50.319 --> 00:07:54.080
there are bigger things to worry about—

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.639
like the threat of a Russian invasion of

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:58.639
Ukraine. And he's been visiting Kyiv for

00:07:56.639 --> 00:08:00.960
talks about that. And then there's all

00:07:58.639 --> 00:08:02.479
the other stuff going on back home. 

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:37.599
So the pressure is on for Prime Minister

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:39.919
Johnson—from the police, the public, the

00:08:37.599 --> 00:08:42.159
media, the opposition from his own

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:44.000
Conservative Party. And there's pressure

00:08:42.159 --> 00:08:45.519
to release the full version of Sue

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.160
Gray's report.

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:49.600
Question is, can his political career

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:51.519
survive?

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:53.360
Hi, if you haven't already seen our

00:08:51.519 --> 00:08:55.440
recent explainer on what's happening

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.680
with Russia and Ukraine. We've linked it

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.920
here for you in the meantime. Make sure

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:01.920
to subscribe to this YouTube channel so

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:06.600
that you don't miss our upcoming Start

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.600
Here episodes and I'll see you next week

